    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok i get the theory side. but in real life, sometimes there's just... weirdness. like a random car stalling or a delivery truck blocking a lane for no clear reason, or just these tiny little disruptions that don't show up in the big data patterns. is there really no way to quantify that kind of \"chaos\" or unpredictable behavior in the modeling?",
