      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Those are difficult to capture, but researchers have attempted to model \"chaos\" in transportation using techniques like stochastic simulations, agent-based modeling, and machine learning. These approaches can account for uncertainties and non-routine events through the use of probabilistic distributions and random variable inputs. However, quantifying and reproducibly reproducing \"weirdness\" in real-world traffic is extremely challenging, if not impossible, with current data-driven modeling tools.",
      "source": "target",
